    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Cal Raleigh** stands as our premier offensive anchor with a score of 78.97. He benefits from a generous matchup against Sugano (4.91 xERA) and a massive 14% park factor boost, making him our highest-projected source of counting stats. **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (66.07) remains an elite start, bolstered by his prime spot in the two-hole and an 85% stolen base success rate against a slow-working pitcher, which aligns with our organizational priority of hunting scarce speed. We are also leaning into **Bryce Harper** (64.58) and **JJ Bleday** (63.38); **Bleday** in particular is a high-conviction play today, capitalizing on a 14% platoon edge against Peterson, while **Harper** continues to drive value through his high-end xwOBA, despite facing a middle-of-the-road arm in Tong.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision involved our utility spot, where **Dylan Beavers** (55.80) edged out **Zack Gelof** (39.57). While **Zack Gelof** was considered, his sub-40 floor score\u2014driven by a difficult matchup against Williams (2.91 xERA) and a negative platoon split\u2014left him on the outside looking in. Conversely, **Dylan Beavers** secured his place in the lineup primarily due to his leadoff role and an opportunistic 16% park factor, which helps mitigate the risk of facing a high-skill arm like Misiorowski. We are also closely monitoring **Jeremiah Jackson** (46.95), who is currently our most volatile start; while the park factor keeps him above the benching threshold, his -19% SP skill penalty suggests a low ceiling against a dominant pitcher. Managers should be prepared for potential underperformance from the middle infield today if Misiorowski commands the zone effectively.",
